WEBVTT

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.370
Green clouds. Red rain.

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:44.810
Impossible.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:47.010
Do you need an explanation?

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:52.450
Tonight at midnight, the Maihama
server's going to be reset.

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:55.990
The people in the city,
along with their memories,

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:58.390
will go back to what
they were 149 days ago.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:02.060
You were told, then?
Well, that saves me the trouble.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.200
Yes.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:07.190
The quantum computer isn't a magic box.

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:09.610
A special characteristic of them is that...

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:12.510
they can't maintain their data
unless they run constantly.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:15.480
Also, new Cerebrants
wouldn't be born, either.

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:20.450
But the data requirements for a
5 kilometer radius virtual world...

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:22.350
and 400 people are enormous.

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:24.990
In addition, people grow and change,

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:27.920
and then the data quickly
expands towards infinity.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:31.590
That's when breakdown
and collapse occurs.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:38.000
And so you have to reset it all,
before the world blows out completely.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.640
There're no exceptions.

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:42.200
The same time period
repeats in an endless loop.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.170
And so the second semester
here in Maihama...

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.840
The morning of September
first never comes!

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:52.640
Living in a world with no
advancement or growth...

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:55.740
The price of eternal life.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:57.880
Not eternal.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:02.720
The server's still a machine,
and machines break down eventually.

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:05.760
You mean...
Then what's the point of all this?!

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.730
To preserve us until the day of rebirth.
Nothing more.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:10.130
Rebirth?!

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:12.500
Can we bring humanity back?!

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:13.940
How?!

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:16.400
The Gards-orm know the method.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:18.670
But we don't.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:22.140
There's no point getting
disappointed over this.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:25.380
This is our reality.
You just forgot about it.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.220
As for Ryoko Kaminagi...

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:34.490
She'll be reinserted into the
Maihama server when it resets.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:38.760
I've given you your explanation.
Now, if you'll excuse me...

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:51.210
<i>Well? How did it feel to explain</i>
<i>it out of your own mouth?</i>

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:53.770
<i>Now you have some idea of how I felt.</i>

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:57.200
We're in a meeting now.
I'll file a report on my feelings later.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:00.220
Let's continue.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:01.750
Sorry I'm late.

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:02.820
Let's begin.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:04.620
You sure you want to leave Kyo alone?

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:07.760
You're my partner now.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.950
You're a strong girl.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:16.960
<i>No. It's because I'm weak.</i>

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.740
<i>A reset.</i>

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:22.640
<i>It's not death or vanishing.</i>

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:25.640
<i>It's just returning to what we were.</i>

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.340
<i>But only I will know.</i>

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.270
<i>About our looping world.</i>
<i>Our infinite hell.</i>

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:33.540
<i>That's crueler than dying.</i>

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:36.190
<i>The ones who aren't aware of it are spared.</i>

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:39.480
<i>Except... No. There are the</i>
<i>ones who experience déjà vu.</i>

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:42.620
<i>And someday,</i>
<i>something may break, and then...</i>

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:49.990
Don't look at me like that!

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:57.600
I also hate it when this time rolls around.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:02.010
It's because we Cerebrants are
exempt from the rules of the reset...

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.210
and retain our memories of the past.

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:08.080
Always having to relive the same activities,
the same life, over and over.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:11.020
It gets so I just want to stay in the
student council room all the time.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.750
I can keep myself
distracted with my duties.

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:17.020
It's an event which will continue
for as long as we live.

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:19.190
All we can do is get used to it.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:23.400
Oh! Why did the commander
leave everything for me to handle?

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.390
Dita, how's the work going?

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:28.840
Maintenance on the
reset system is complete.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:31.410
All adjustments are running fairly well,

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:34.480
but a few delays have cropped
up on our optimization work.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:37.600
Hurry! We only have
eight hours till the reset.

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:40.380
Fosetta, what's the status
of the Maihama server?

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:42.220
No lethal failures detected.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:45.150
We're still trying hard to
stabilize the environmental data.

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:47.920
Ricerca, what's the latest patrol sit-rep?

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:50.990
Not a single enemy blip
within a 100 kilometer radius!

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:53.000
Keep a sharp eye out for any.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.400
Our Pellucidar mode and the
Zegas are down for repairs.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.170
The Oceanus is practically unarmed.

00:05:57.170 --> 00:05:58.220
Yes, yes.

00:05:58.300 --> 00:05:59.460
One "yes," if you please!

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:04.860
We'll have the new weapons to counter
the Anti-Zega mounted on the Altair soon.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:08.780
Repairs on the Garuda and Hraesvelg
will take a bit longer, though.

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:12.010
Due to the appearance of the Anti-Zega,

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:14.810
the Zegapain's qualitative
superiority has been wiped away.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:18.750
A drastic revamping of our
tactics has become necessary.

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:23.120
I'm not usually one to gamble,
but you're saying we have no choice.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:24.530
Well, then...

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.720
You're going to try it? The final plan?

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:29.200
Within the next three months.

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:40.610
What's this?

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:46.710
From me?

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:53.450
My diary?

00:06:56.130 --> 00:07:00.260
This entry's for today.
"August 31st. This day has come yet again."

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:03.960
"This endlessly repeating world...
I'm sick of it."

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:08.800
"I pray that I don't understand
the meaning of these words."

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:13.330
"Once I've done this, they'll restore me
and I'll become a Cerebrant again."

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:16.380
This is me! The old me.

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:19.280
"I don't want to become one of them again."

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:21.850
"And so I've left messages
for my future self."

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:28.380
"This is the fifth time I've reached
'today' since becoming a Cerebrant."

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:30.350
"How about you?"

00:07:31.490 --> 00:07:33.050
Shut up, you idiot.

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:40.830
Good evening, Sogoru.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:43.510
Here, check this out!

00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:46.440
Izumi-sempai wrote me a love letter!

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:51.510
Still, even if I wrote her back,
she'd never get it, would she?

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:57.550
It's not like we're dying,
but it's still kind of sad.

00:07:57.550 --> 00:08:00.390
I don't think we'll be able
to keep our memories.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:05.020
That's why we figured we'd spend
this last night with you, Sogoru.

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:06.900
You guys...

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:08.950
I called Kawaguchi
and Ushio to come, too.

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:12.260
It's the last night of summer break.
Let's have some fun!

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:17.430
Shut up!

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:21.810
This is from the entrance ceremony!
God, we all look like little kids!

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:23.110
You're right.

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:26.550
A lot happened to us over
the last five months, didn't it?

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:28.550
There I am!

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:29.550
I look cool!

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:30.420
How?!

00:08:31.890 --> 00:08:34.010
And there's Kyo. Lame!

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:35.850
Who are you callin' lame?!

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:38.960
Well, it's time you cheered up!

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:44.000
The Maihama Minami high school swim
club's gonna sweep the championship!

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.560
Tomorrow, we start special training to do it!

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:48.500
Tomorrow?

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.510
Kaminagi took these, right?

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:58.480
Who else do you think
would have taken them?

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:00.280
I wish she could have come tonight, too.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:03.320
Forget it! Ryoko never goes out
at night to have fun.

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:05.340
Well, we'll see her tomorrow.

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:06.920
Yeah, but tomorrow...

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:09.360
Aw, man...

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:13.320
Tomorrow, we'll have forgotten everything
and have to rerun that whole fight we had.

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:15.520
What a drag.

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:19.470
You and I can become
friends again, right, Sogoru?

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:20.160
Sure.

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:22.960
What are you guys talking about?

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:27.570
On this occasion,
I have one thing to say to you!

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:29.910
Huh? What's with you?

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:32.280
Kyo, you're strong.

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:35.610
And being strong, you hold
everything in till it wears you out!

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:39.610
Look, try to depend on
the rest of us a little more.

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:41.750
You can't win a race all by yourself.

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:46.090
Even in a medley relay, <i>everyone</i>
contributes to the winning time.

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:50.030
I agree!

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:54.400
Do your best at whatever you're doing,
and be satisfied with that.

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:57.500
Ushio... Kawaguchi...

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:03.140
I think... Maybe we should
suffer a little more.

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:07.620
They say pain ultimately
leads to happiness.

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:11.050
Without some pain,
you can never achieve true happiness.

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:14.420
Pain that leads to happiness, huh?

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:16.430
Just kidding!

00:10:16.430 --> 00:10:18.590
That's just something
I read in a ladies comic!

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:22.860
Did I get too pretentious?

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:24.800
Hey, guys! How about a swim?

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:26.540
Yeah! Sounds great!

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:27.740
I'm game!

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:29.440
Oh, what the hell. I'll join in!

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:30.130
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:37.280
On your mark!

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:38.770
Get set...

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:40.710
Start!

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:41.950
Come on!

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:07.530
Ushio!

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:20.990
Come on!

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:24.490
Kawaguchi!

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.740
Holy! You're about to
break the school record!

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:42.040
Hang in there!

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:46.840
Kyo!

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:39.930
Guys...

00:12:56.990 --> 00:13:02.820
Sogoru!

00:13:03.890 --> 00:13:05.930
I'm glad we're going to be in the same class!

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:22.140
<i>I'll protect you.</i>

00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:25.180
<i>Until the day you're reborn. All of you!</i>

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:45.690
Hey, Tomigai. Where's Kaminagi?

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:48.470
I haven't seen her around here.

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:51.140
Sogoru, what are you talking about?

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:55.540
Where is she?! Come on!

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:58.150
Where's the hospital Kaminagi's been sent to?!

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:01.640
What's with you, kid? You just got into school
and you're already trying to start fights?!

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:04.350
Kaminagi and I grew up together!

00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:08.650
I see. I'm terribly sorry for you.

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:14.620
Awful, how she got in that traffic accident on
spring break, right before entering school...

00:14:14.860 --> 00:14:15.660
Traffic accident?

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:20.670
What the hell is this?!

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:24.660
Kaminagi, what's wrong with you?!
Answer me, Kaminagi!

00:14:25.870 --> 00:14:27.270
It's no use.

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:30.350
The data salvage was successful.

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:32.380
However, we weren't able
to restore her...

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:34.810
to the level of a normally-
functioning meta-body.

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:43.530
Ryoko is?!

00:14:43.530 --> 00:14:44.490
Oh, no.

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:48.560
This is the first I've heard about it!

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:51.120
She has enough data left for a
perfectly usable personality.

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:55.430
But, when we try and forcibly
restore it, we get an error cascade.

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:57.770
Her personality collapses.

00:14:57.940 --> 00:14:59.630
And Ryoko disappears.

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:04.910
This is impossible. It can't be...

00:15:06.310 --> 00:15:07.110
Why?

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:10.790
Why did you bring her back?

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:12.510
For Kyo's sake.

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:14.820
And is Kyo happy about this?

00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:16.390
Is Ryoko?!

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:20.030
I was the one who found
her data in the first place!

00:15:20.030 --> 00:15:22.230
Do you think I could just delete her?!

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:23.750
Even if it's just a fragment of her left!

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:29.370
I'm not as strong as Shima is.

00:15:30.140 --> 00:15:32.610
I couldn't tell him. Not Kyo...

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:37.700
Mr. President, when?!
When will Kaminagi wake up?!

00:15:41.150 --> 00:15:42.740
She will if you want her to.

00:15:43.390 --> 00:15:47.690
Quantum energy reaction at 11 o'clock.
Range: 98,000.

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:49.660
It's Anti-Zega Coatlicue!

00:15:51.060 --> 00:15:54.050
Sound battle stations!
Take the Oceanus into the cloud bank!

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:05.470
Hey! Kaminagi! Where is she?!

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:07.370
Kyo, board Zegapain.

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:10.030
Once you're aboard,
you'll understand everything.

00:16:20.090 --> 00:16:21.660
Can we deploy the Zegas?

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:25.020
We can send out the Altair only.
However, it hasn't been tested yet!

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:26.920
It's an emergency. We'll omit the tests.

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:28.390
May-yu and I will go out!

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:30.730
That won't be necessary.

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:35.030
Hi, Kyo.

00:16:39.270 --> 00:16:41.570
I've missed you. All this time.

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:42.810
Kaminagi...

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:43.510
It's Ryoko!

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:52.790
<i>System check!</i>

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:53.890
<i>All green!</i>

00:16:53.890 --> 00:16:56.890
<i>Countdown starting! Transmission</i>
<i>scatter rate, confirmed.</i>

00:16:56.890 --> 00:16:59.090
<i>Bednorz parameter, stable.</i>

00:16:59.090 --> 00:17:01.100
<i>Bednorz curve, holding.</i>

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:03.030
Restoration coordinates, set and locked!

00:17:03.030 --> 00:17:04.130
K- Kaminagi...

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:05.760
We can talk later! Here we go!

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:07.200
How can you?!

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:11.040
If we don't defeat the Anti-Zega,
everyone's going to die, Kyo!

00:17:12.470 --> 00:17:13.840
<i>Altair, transmit!</i>

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:15.070
Entangle!

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:23.850
Holonic field, forming!

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:25.720
Holonic Launcher!

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:32.430
Here comes that light armor canceler!

00:17:32.430 --> 00:17:33.760
That won't work anymore!

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:41.370
It's blocking it.

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:43.910
By constantly varying
the light armor's phase,

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:45.870
we render the canceler useless!

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:48.300
Kaminagi!

00:18:03.460 --> 00:18:04.650
The launcher!

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:06.860
It's okay! I'll have it fixed in a sec!

00:18:06.860 --> 00:18:10.990
Cutting power circuits 210 to 228!
Rerouting 36 to 193!

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:16.230
Bypassing 47 to 115!
Power systems check: green!

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:18.440
Power, restored! Sorry for the delay!

00:18:18.440 --> 00:18:19.570
Thank you!

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:24.580
He's a match for the Anti-Zega!

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:26.570
They're good. Kyo <i>and</i> Ryoko.

00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:28.970
But why is she awake?

00:18:29.950 --> 00:18:33.320
It's only when she's fighting in the Zega.

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:35.420
Then she turns back to the old Ryoko.

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:38.760
We're running out of Q.L.!

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:41.590
Kyo! We need to finish it off all
at once with the new weapon!

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:44.460
I'll send you the data on it now!

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:49.960
What the?!

00:18:51.470 --> 00:18:52.460
Gotcha, Kaminagi!

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:06.620
We just have one chance.

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:09.110
Use all our remaining Q.L. and hit that thing!

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:10.520
Leave it to me!

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:22.140
<i>Powerful energy collecting in head of Coatlicue.</i>

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:22.900
Him, too?!

00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:24.370
Like I care?!

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:27.510
Holo-Bolt Pressure!

00:19:34.250 --> 00:19:36.050
Not good enough!

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:53.170
Are you okay, Kaminagi?!

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:55.860
Yeah. What about the Anti-Zega?

00:19:56.300 --> 00:19:58.000
He's out of power, too.

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:04.350
Abyss... He survived, too?

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:06.480
Where...

00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:10.940
Where will our battle... finally end?

00:20:15.890 --> 00:20:18.220
We couldn't achieve a perfect integration.

00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:23.350
Her quantum data that remains in
the Altair's meta-body buffer is...

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:29.560
There was too much hardware damage and
data corruption during the transmission.

00:20:30.510 --> 00:20:32.470
This is the best we could do.

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:34.470
Oh, no...

00:20:34.780 --> 00:20:37.900
Lovers who can only be
together on the battlefield.

00:20:38.580 --> 00:20:40.950
How will she live from now on?

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:45.740
Her only option...
is to grow as Kyo's partner.

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:49.020
You brought her back like this...

00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:51.920
because you need her to fight.
Is that it, Commander?!

00:21:01.770 --> 00:21:04.800
Oh, Kyo... Look at me.

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:07.730
Look what I've become!

00:21:11.710 --> 00:21:13.700
<i>The pain that leads to happiness...</i>

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:18.450
<i>How much suffering will it take</i>
<i>to lead to happiness in the end?</i>

00:22:51.650 --> 00:22:55.320
How?! How was Sin able to
get on board the Oceanus?!

00:22:55.320 --> 00:22:57.120
She doesn't seem to have any weapons with her.

00:22:57.120 --> 00:22:59.090
What's she after?!

00:22:59.090 --> 00:23:00.960
She says she can't see the light?

00:23:00.960 --> 00:23:02.290
Is it possible?

00:23:02.290 --> 00:23:04.520
She doesn't understand why
we humans are fighting them?!

00:23:05.130 --> 00:23:07.730
No, stop... Stay away from Kaminagi!

00:23:07.730 --> 00:23:11.390
Against these restored flesh and
blood creatures, we're totally helpless!

00:23:12.230 --> 00:23:15.860
Next time, on Zegapain:
"The Reconstructants."

00:23:16.000 --> 00:23:18.340
My pain, never to be forgotten.
